__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.gitignore
.claude
# DB dumps and the collectstatic output (rebuilt by `manage.py bootstrap`
# at container start — a host copy would ship stale assets).
backups/
staticfiles/
*.zip
# The slide deck IS app code: the GUI's "About starcubes" menu links to
# /slides, and viz.views.slides streams repo-root presentation.html plus
# its assets under presentation/.
*.md
# ...and so is the documentation: /help/ renders these files at request time
# (core/docs.py), so an image without them serves a help section of 404s
# while a developer's checkout works perfectly.
#
# Mind the matching rule, which is not glob-in-a-shell: `*` does not cross a
# `/`, so the `*.md` above only ever caught the four repo-root files. That is
# why docs/*.md has always been in the image (needs no exception here — the
# one below is documentation of intent, not a functional line) and why the
# per-app CLAUDE.md files were too, until the explicit `**` pattern. Verified
# by building a throwaway context and listing the layer.
**/CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!HOWTO.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!docs/*.md
.dockerignore
Dockerfile_orig
__pycache__
*.egg-info
.eggs
*.sqlc
*.log
logs/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# Top-level node_modules from `npm install` — installed at build time by the
# jsbuilder Dockerfile stage, must not leak into the build context.
node_modules